{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update28.json\",\"summary\":\"Cited the revised authority experiment (receipt 67fc59b525e54d01b709a19592689357) in the configuration-recovery account, closing the reproducibility question opened by the earlier repeat. With the harness enforcing the premise - it keeps committing until A's commit-tracking store reports a non-zero persisted commit index before restarting A - the witness reappeared: event 15 records staged commit index 4 with no extra applies needed and no tracked configuration (latest index 0, no members), and event 16 shows zero candidate samples in the 1500ms window while the control that recovered its configuration was a candidate in 257 samples (event 18), comparisons violated and holds. The same receipt re-observed the commit-rule, durable-snapshot and availability cases with the same operands (events 4, 6-8, 11, 13). The account now cites six receipts, states the precondition (a non-zero persisted commit index in the caller's store) as part of the authority claim with both valid executions reporting it, keeps the earlier non-applicable repeat as counterevidence for the other side of the condition, and replaces the 'single valid witness' limitation with the remaining honest boundary that the precondition comes from caller-side store behaviour.\"}"}}
